			<item>
				<title>Play moview with DTS audio on Chromecast</title>
				<link>https://kowalcj0.github.io/2019/06/09/cast-dts-movie-to-chromecast/</link>
				<pubDate>Sun, 09 Jun 2019 20:35:50 +0100</pubDate>
				<guid>https://kowalcj0.github.io/2019/06/09/cast-dts-movie-to-chromecast/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;According to the official &lt;a href=&#34;https://developers.google.com/cast/docs/media&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;specification&lt;/a&gt; &lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 12 16&#34; width=&#34;12&#34; height=&#34;16&#34;&gt;&lt;path fill-rule=&#34;evenodd&#34; d=&#34;M11 10h1v3c0 .55-.45 1-1 1H1c-.55 0-1-.45-1-1V3c0-.55.45-1 1-1h3v1H1v10h10v-3zM6 2l2.25 2.25L5 7.5 6.5 9l3.25-3.25L12 8V2H6z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;&#xA;Chromecast (even Ultra version) doesn&amp;rsquo;t support DTS.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If you can&amp;rsquo;t be bothered to spend few hours to transcode the movie with lets&#xA;say &lt;a href=&#34;https://handbrake.fr/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;Handbrake&lt;/a&gt; &lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 12 16&#34; width=&#34;12&#34; height=&#34;16&#34;&gt;&lt;path fill-rule=&#34;evenodd&#34; d=&#34;M11 10h1v3c0 .55-.45 1-1 1H1c-.55 0-1-.45-1-1V3c0-.55.45-1 1-1h3v1H1v10h10v-3zM6 2l2.25 2.25L5 7.5 6.5 9l3.25-3.25L12 8V2H6z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA; you can use ver handy CLI casting tool: &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/xat/castnow&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;castnow&lt;/a&gt; &lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 12 16&#34; width=&#34;12&#34; height=&#34;16&#34;&gt;&lt;path fill-rule=&#34;evenodd&#34; d=&#34;M11 10h1v3c0 .55-.45 1-1 1H1c-.55 0-1-.45-1-1V3c0-.55.45-1 1-1h3v1H1v10h10v-3zM6 2l2.25 2.25L5 7.5 6.5 9l3.25-3.25L12 8V2H6z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Tasty smoothie - no. 1</title>
				<link>https://kowalcj0.github.io/2019/05/18/tasty-smothie-no-1/</link>
				<pubDate>Sat, 18 May 2019 19:44:50 +0100</pubDate>
				<guid>https://kowalcj0.github.io/2019/05/18/tasty-smothie-no-1/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;A simple recipe for a delicious smoothie.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;ingredients&#34;&gt;Ingredients:&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;50-80g yoghurt&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;100ml milk (regular, soy or oat etc.)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;1 medium banana&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;1 passion fruit&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;1 small lime&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;few raspberries&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;few blueberries&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;2-4 strawberries&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;water to top it up&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;extras&#34;&gt;Extras:&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;You might add:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;jam (for some extra flavour)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;ispaghula husk (e.g &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.boots.com/fybogel-hi-fibre-orange-30-sachets-10052725&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;Fybogel orange flavour&lt;/a&gt; &lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 12 16&#34; width=&#34;12&#34; height=&#34;16&#34;&gt;&lt;path fill-rule=&#34;evenodd&#34; d=&#34;M11 10h1v3c0 .55-.45 1-1 1H1c-.55 0-1-.45-1-1V3c0-.55.45-1 1-1h3v1H1v10h10v-3zM6 2l2.25 2.25L5 7.5 6.5 9l3.25-3.25L12 8V2H6z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;) - for those with IBS&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Logrotate your bash history file</title>
				<link>https://kowalcj0.github.io/2019/05/13/logrotate-bash-history/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 13 May 2019 11:50:50 +0100</pubDate>
				<guid>https://kowalcj0.github.io/2019/05/13/logrotate-bash-history/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;A while ago I decided to take more control over my bash history and I followed&#xA;this advice &lt;a href=&#34;https://unix.stackexchange.com/a/48113&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;https://unix.stackexchange.com/a/48113&lt;/a&gt; &lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 12 16&#34; width=&#34;12&#34; height=&#34;16&#34;&gt;&lt;path fill-rule=&#34;evenodd&#34; d=&#34;M11 10h1v3c0 .55-.45 1-1 1H1c-.55 0-1-.45-1-1V3c0-.55.45-1 1-1h3v1H1v10h10v-3zM6 2l2.25 2.25L5 7.5 6.5 9l3.25-3.25L12 8V2H6z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;With time I&amp;rsquo;ve tweaked few settings, like ignore lines that start with space,&#xA;and ignore some of the trivial commands like &lt;code&gt;ls&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;export HISTCONTROL=ignoredups:erasedups:ignorespace     # no duplicate entries &amp;amp; lines starting with space&#xA;export HISTSIZE=99999999                                # big big history&#xA;export HISTFILESIZE=99999999                            # big big history&#xA;shopt -s histappend                                     # append to history, don&amp;#39;t overwrite it&#xA;export PROMPT_COMMAND=&amp;#34;history -a; history -c; history -r; $PROMPT_COMMAND&amp;#34;  # Save and reload the history after each command finishes&#xA;HISTIGNORE=&amp;#39;ll *:ls *:l:gs:&amp;#39;                            # ignore some commands&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;Nevertheless, every now and then I&amp;rsquo;d loose the command history, e.g. when&#xA;upgrading the distro. I then discovered &lt;a href=&#34;https://linux.die.net/man/8/logrotate&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;logrotate&lt;/a&gt; &lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 12 16&#34; width=&#34;12&#34; height=&#34;16&#34;&gt;&lt;path fill-rule=&#34;evenodd&#34; d=&#34;M11 10h1v3c0 .55-.45 1-1 1H1c-.55 0-1-.45-1-1V3c0-.55.45-1 1-1h3v1H1v10h10v-3zM6 2l2.25 2.25L5 7.5 6.5 9l3.25-3.25L12 8V2H6z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;.&#xA;It&amp;rsquo;s a brilliant and easy to use tool for, guess what, log rotation!&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
	</channel>
